Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:02.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}They buried a body\Nas China's emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.07,0:00:03.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}His own uncle
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.86,0:00:05.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}kept searching for him.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.89,0:00:08.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}The missing emperor\Nwas Jianwen.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.43,0:00:11.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}His grandfather had\Nfounded the Ming dynasty.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.50,0:00:13.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}But Jianwen inherited\Nsomething else:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.23,0:00:15.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}uncles with armies.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.83,0:00:17.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}When he tried
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.43,0:00:19.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}to take away\Ntheir power,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.23,0:00:20.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}one uncle, Zhu Di,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.87,0:00:21.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}rebelled.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.79,0:00:23.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}Three years later,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.01,0:00:25.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}Zhu Di reached Nanjing.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.31,0:00:27.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}A commander who had once
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.73,0:00:28.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}fought for Jianwen
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.91,0:00:30.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}helped open a city gate.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.08,0:00:33.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}Then the palace\Ncaught fire.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.36,0:00:35.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}Zhu Di's men\Ncarried out a body.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.79,0:00:37.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}He had it buried\Nas his nephew.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.12,0:00:41.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}Jianwen's small son\Nvanished too. Zhu Di
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.19,0:00:42.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}took the throne\Nas Yongle,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.66,0:00:45.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}and wiped Jianwen's\Nreign from the calendar.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.53,0:00:48.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}But rumours said\NJianwen had escaped,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.38,0:00:49.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}dressed as a monk.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.86,0:00:51.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}Yongle sent an official
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.22,0:00:53.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}named Hu Ying\Nacross China.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.54,0:00:54.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}Officially,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.24,0:00:56.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}he was seeking a\NDaoist holy man.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.02,0:00:59.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}Secretly, he was\Nlooking for Jianwen.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.13,0:01:01.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}When Hu Ying's\Nmother died,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.04,0:01:03.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}he asked to go home.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.93,0:01:05.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}Yongle refused.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.53,0:01:07.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}More than twenty\Nyears after the fire,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.97,0:01:09.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}Hu Ying returned.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.75,0:01:11.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}Yongle was\Nalready in bed.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.72,0:01:12.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}He got up,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.77,0:01:14.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}summoned the official,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.14,0:01:16.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}and listened until\Ndeep into the night.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.11,0:01:18.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}The later\NHistory of Ming
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.77,0:01:21.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}says Yongle's suspicions\Nfinally ended.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.34,0:01:23.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}It never says
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.19,0:01:24.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,80)}what Hu Ying told him.
